h->next of the Content-Encoding line of the zstd filter set (NULL): since nginx
1.23.0 the header lines are linked by it and nginx sets it for every line it
makes (ngx_http_gzip_filter_module.c); the module (sysadmin-labs 0.1.3) left it
as ngx_list_push() gave it, not initialized, for whatever follows the link.
Applied by post-patch in WRKSRC_zstd after extra-patch-zstd-accept-encoding, -p0.

--- src/ngx_http_zstd_filter_module.c.orig
+++ src/ngx_http_zstd_filter_module.c
@@ -264,6 +264,7 @@
     }
 
     h->hash = 1;
+    h->next = NULL;
     ngx_str_set(&h->key, "Content-Encoding");
     ngx_str_set(&h->value, "zstd");
     r->headers_out.content_encoding = h;
